# Build-context exclusions for the three images built from THIS directory
# (infra/compose sets `context: ../..` for api, provisioner and web).
#
# There was no such file, and the one that exists — apps/web/.dockerignore — never applied:
# Docker reads `.dockerignore` at the CONTEXT ROOT, and the context root is here, not
# apps/web. Measured rather than assumed, with a throwaway build in a scratch directory on
# the Docker running this machine (29.6.1): a `.dockerignore` beside the Dockerfile is
# ignored, and so is the `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` convention; only a file at the context
# root changed what `COPY` picked up.
#
# So `COPY apps/web/ ./` in apps/web/Dockerfile was copying apps/web/node_modules — on top of
# the `npm install` the stage had just run — and any apps/web/.env with it, and the whole tree
# below (including infra/compose/.env, which holds the real secrets) was being scanned and
# offered to the daemon on every build.
#
# Every path a Dockerfile here COPYs is deliberately still included:
#   api          native/{package.json,package-lock.json,Cargo.toml,Cargo.lock,build.rs,src,core},
#                apps/api/{package.json,src}, packages/db
#   provisioner  apps/provisioner/{package.json,src}, packages/db
#   web          apps/web/ (whole), packages/bmd, packages/bmd-editor

# Installed dependencies — re-installed inside every image from the lockfile.
**/node_modules

# Secrets. Nothing here is COPYed by any Dockerfile; they were only ever exposure.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Build output. Every image builds its own; a stale host copy would only shadow it.
**/dist
**/target
**/.vite
**/build

# History, tooling and local state.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
